PPC — Programming Cycling Coach
Copyright 2024-2026 PPC

This product includes software developed from Domestique (original Apache-2.0
project, v3.5.2), a cycling training planner + workout library + post-ride
viewer. The original Domestique codebase, build system, and much of the
training science engine are reused under the Apache License 2.0.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCIENTIFIC ATTRIBUTIONS (training & nutrition models embedded in this app)
----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Strength & mobility programming
  - Llanos-Lagos, T. et al. (2025). Concurrent training: strength prescription
    for endurance athletes. Eur J Appl Physiol. (basis for 2x/week, 4x6 @ 85%
    1RM gym block.)
  - Vikmoen, O. et al. (2021). Strength training and endurance performance.
  - Warneke, K. et al. (2025). Mobility / range-of-motion training and
    endurance-athlete injury risk (basis for the daily mobility routine).

Nutrition & supplementation
  - GSSI Sport Science Exchange (SSE) 231: Carbohydrate periodization for
    endurance athletes (basis for the carb-periodization model).
  - Jeukendrup, A. & UCI Sports Nutrition Project (2026): race-fueling
    carbohydrate + caffeine guidelines (basis for the race-day fueling block).
  - Supplement "Gruppo A" evidence tiers follow established sports-nutrition
    consensus (caffeine, beta-alanine, nitrate, bicarbonate, creatine, glycerol).

Training-load & periodization science (inherited from Domestique)
  - Mujika, I. & Padilla, S. (2003). Tapering for competition.
  - Gabbett, T.J. (2016). Training-load spikes and injury risk (ACWR).
  - Banister, E.W. (1991). Training impulse / fitness-fatigue (CTL/TSB model).
  - Seiler, S. (2010). Polarized training distribution.

